art (see fig). A listener, located at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></math>, directly in front of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>, finds that the intensity is at a minimum when he is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> away from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>. The listener moves away from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>, keeping the distance from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> fixed. The adjacent maximum of intensity is observed when the listener is at a distance&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi></math> from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>. Then&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi></math> is :</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F113217a9-d679-4107-b163-25ef4f184085-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 218px; height: 220px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "5f2290", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef6c677dc36a88f3658"}, {"id": "5e3132", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef6c677dc36a88f3659"}, {"id": "966a4a", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef6c677dc36a88f365a"}, {"id": "44fdde", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</