ane of slits. If the screen is moved by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> towards the slits, the change in fringe width is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>. If the distance between the slits is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mm</mi></math>, then the wavelength of the light will be____<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>nm</mi></math>."}, "options": [{"id": "5c7b5e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef6c677dc36a88f36a3"}, {"id": "2bb3ed", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef6c677dc36a88f36a4"}, {"id": "50f3f4", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef6c677dc36a88f36a5"}, {"id": "416f85", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef6c677dc36a88f36a6"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef6c677dc36a88f36a7", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60da9b5062f042332c53835a"], "topics": ["6117b5e7478ae845c43c5ee8"], "concepts": ["6117b5e3478ae845c43c5dfa"], "question": {"text": "Orange light of wavelength&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6000</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>m</mi></math>&nbsp;illuminates a single slit of width&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>m</mi></math>.&nbsp;The maximum possible number of diffraction minima produced on both sides of the central maximum is __________"}, "options": [{"id": "53b612", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef6c677dc36a88f36a8"}, {"id": "e5cf49", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4e